      independent_thinking: [70, 0.5, "s", "A"],
      // [src_ibsen_brit, src_ibsen_uio, src_ibsen_scandinavica, src_ibsen_freebeacon | 1866-1890 | reference + institution + scholarly review + critic] Britannica says he introduced to the European stage a new order of moral analysis against a realistic middle-class background, and the Oslo centre says his contemporary plays put him at the forefront of the modern breakthrough and laid the foundation for the modern theatre; the Scandinavica reviewer's note on how he managed publication and performances and the critical Free Beacon essay (the stock characters now feel familiar) show the judgement is contested in degree. The claim is by reference and institutional assessment, not by close reading of the plays, so confidence is moderate.
