      systems_abstraction: [74, 0.58, "s", "A"],
      // [src_thompson_ritchie, src_thompson_pike, src_thompson_linfo | 1969-1992 | collaborator history + collaborator account + reference biography] Ritchie says Thompson turned an intended week-long Fortran effort into the language B and that he built the first file system, shell and assembler on the PDP-7; Pike says Thompson wrote the UTF-8 packing code the night of the diner meeting and Plan 9 ran only UTF-8 within days; the reference biography says the first system took about a month. All three are admiring collaborator recollections or a secondary compilation with exact durations unverified. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): first-pass 78 / 0.62 lowered to 72 / 0.54 because the speed claims rest on Pike's 2003 recollection and an unsourced reference-site summary rather than dated records.
      execution_speed: [72, 0.54, "d", "A"],
      // [src_thompson_ritchie, src_thompson_chmblog, src_thompson_wired | 1969-1970 | collaborator history + museum blog + press profile] After Bell Labs' withdrawal from Multics and repeated failed requests for a new machine, Ritchie says Thompson found a little-used PDP-7 and built an operating system; the CHM blog and Wired both report he started it on his own initiative and Wired says he wrote Unix mainly for his own use. Consistent across three source types; initiative is documented, though the account of motive partly rests on Thompson's own words.
      proactive_agency: [72, 0.58, "d", "A"],
      // [src_thompson_wired, src_thompson_chmblog, src_thompson_ritchie | 1969-1995 | press profile + museum blog + collaborator history] Wired says his career was guided by his own 'quixotic impulses', that he treats his private office as a mail drop, that he said bug reports were sometimes ignored since maintaining Unix was not his job, and that he valued Bell Labs' freedom to do whatever he wanted; the CHM blog quotes him crediting unconstrained research; Ritchie records Space Travel and Unix growing from personal itches. The cost side (users' complaints about terseness, ignored reports) makes it dual-edged; much of the motive comes from his own remarks to one journalist.
      autonomy_need: [72, 0.56, "d", "D"],
