      deep_focus: [66, 0.5, "d", "A"],
      // [src_thompson_trust, src_thompson_pike, src_thompson_wired, src_thompson_gofaq | 1969-2009 | self lecture + collaborator account + press profile + team history] He opens his Turing lecture crediting Ritchie and Unix's many contributors, Pike describes designing UTF-8 together over dinner, Wired shows him rewriting audio code with a younger programmer, and the Go history lists him as one of three founders sketching the language. Mostly his own words and a close collaborator's recollection; no independent view of how he worked day to day with colleagues beyond Wired.
      collaboration: [64, 0.5, "d", "A"],
      // [src_thompson_bell1999, src_thompson_gofaq, src_thompson_ritchie, src_thompson_wired | 1969-2009 | employer release + team history + collaborator history + press profile] Across Space Travel, the Belle chess machine, audio compression and a first Go compiler written 'to explore ideas' he moved between prototypes, and Bell Labs lists operating systems, languages, security, games and digital music among his research. The breadth is well documented; no source describes his experimental method, so the score stays moderate.
      experimentation: [66, 0.52, "d", "A"],
