      leadership_drive: [66, 0.5, "d", "D"],
      // [src_nureyev_ebsco, src_nureyev_nation | 1960s-1980s | encyclopaedia + critical review] EBSCO says he discovered and developed dancers with international careers and was a generous mentor to young artists; The Nation reports Kavanagh's argument that he surpassed Baryshnikov as mentor and promoted young dancers at the Paris Opera. Reasonable inference of investment in the art form beyond his own performances, but only two sources and no detailed episodes.
